WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.253 --> 00:00:05.714
The film CODA - it's the story of a teenage girl

00:00:05.714 --> 00:00:07.465
who has this deaf family.

00:00:07.465 --> 00:00:10.468
There's a scene in the film - this school concert

00:00:10.468 --> 00:00:13.388
and we get to Ruby's performance and right when you're ready

00:00:13.388 --> 00:00:16.349
to hear her we go to complete silence

00:00:16.349 --> 00:00:18.685
and shift POVs to this family.

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:22.355
They are starting to look around to get perspective on

00:00:22.355 --> 00:00:25.442
you know, is she good? Are people enjoying it?

00:00:25.442 --> 00:00:27.736
They go home, they're about to go into the house and

00:00:27.736 --> 00:00:30.071
Frank wants a moment alone out on the truck.

00:00:30.071 --> 00:00:33.408
Ruby sees that moment, and then Frank asks her, 

00:00:33.408 --> 00:00:35.410
“That song you sang tonight, what was it about?"

00:00:35.410 --> 00:00:38.788
It was about

00:00:38.788 --> 00:00:41.249
what it is to need another person.

00:00:41.249 --> 00:00:44.461
The lyrics of that song are really, really resonant.

00:00:44.461 --> 00:00:46.463
In that moment he says, “Can you sing it for me?"

00:00:46.463 --> 00:00:50.508
♫ Like the sweet morning dew ♫

00:00:50.508 --> 00:00:54.679
♫ I took one look at you ♫

00:00:54.679 --> 00:01:01.436
♫ and it was plain to see you were my destiny. ♫

00:01:01.436 --> 00:01:04.773
Frank is trying to understand why...

00:01:04.773 --> 00:01:07.275
What is so special about his daughter's singing?

00:01:07.275 --> 00:01:08.902
Is there something that Frank is missing?

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:11.237
So I wanted that time to find those moments.

00:01:11.237 --> 00:01:13.948
I was grateful that most of the singing, like all of the singing

00:01:13.948 --> 00:01:16.910
was live on set because in one of the takes he was like, “More.

00:01:16.910 --> 00:01:18.828
Louder!" And I didn't know he was going to do that and so then

00:01:18.828 --> 00:01:20.205
I had to sing louder.

00:01:20.205 --> 00:01:23.124
So much of it just came alive on set when we were together.

00:01:24.167 --> 00:01:27.837
I said Troy, you get Emilia to sing loud enough so that you

00:01:27.837 --> 00:01:31.674
can feel something and Emilia, you get him to feel something.

00:01:31.674 --> 00:01:33.343
♫ I will go ♫

00:01:33.343 --> 00:01:35.303
♫ where you lead ♫

00:01:35.303 --> 00:01:38.431
♫ always there in time of need. ♫

00:01:38.431 --> 00:01:41.392
In this moment I, as Frank, had to make a big decision.

00:01:41.392 --> 00:01:44.938
As her father, do I let her go?

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:47.148
It was so emotional what happened.

00:01:47.148 --> 00:01:50.735
It's not that he magically got to have music.

00:01:50.735 --> 00:01:52.904
It's that he had a very intimate

00:01:52.904 --> 00:01:54.656
connected experience with his daughter.

00:01:54.656 --> 00:01:57.117
Of understanding something that she loves.

00:01:57.117 --> 00:01:59.244
And he gave her that moment.

00:01:59.244 --> 00:02:02.789
She busted into tears and everyone on set busted into tears.

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:05.500
It was a great scene to do because so much changed on the day

00:02:05.500 --> 00:02:07.377
and it was kind of we were living it.

00:02:08.211 --> 00:02:11.589
♫ All that I need ♫

00:02:11.589 --> 00:02:15.677
♫ to get by. ♫

